    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1402-a2">

                <pb facs="1107" n="991" xml:id="pg991"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Consul to the
                            American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Fez</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-05-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my letter of yesterday,
                    I have the pleasure to report that M. Gaillard, French Consul, called here
                    yesterday afternoon and, in my presence, told Hadj Mohammed Lehsen that he was
                    satisfied no proceedings whatever against him were in contemplation, and so M.
                    Gaillard assured Hadj Mohammed he might now leave this Consulate freely without
                    fear of molestation.</p>
                <p>M. Gaillard assured me fully that the proceedings still to complete were merely
                    formal and so it would only be causing Hadj Mohammed Lehsen unnecessary
                    inconvenience were he to remain at this Consulate any longer.</p>
                <p>Hadj Mohammed Lehsen, on my explaining this to him, stated he was quite
                    satisfied, and after expressing his best thanks to M. Gaillard and myself he
                    returned with great contentment to his house.</p>
                <p>The incident, as far as it concerns Hadj Mohammed Lehsen, appears, therefore, to
                    be now ended. I hope that I have been fortunate enough to act about it in the
                    way your excellency would wish.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. M. Macleod.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
